<title>SINGAPORE: CM Telecom buys two Hong Kong properties.</title>
<headline>CM Telecom buys two Hong Kong properties.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>CM Telecom International Limited said on Monday it was buying two shops in Hong Kong for HK$46.5 million to expand its retail telecommunications business.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement it was buying one shop at Lai Yuen Apartments in Causeway Bay for HK$23.5 million. It said the second, at Commercial Podium, Sincere House in Kowloon, was being acquired from Headson Rise Limited for HK$23 million.</p>
<p>It said the shops were being bought through subsidiaries and it would finance the purchases from internal resources and bank borrowings.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
